        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mark Rylance, Rudolf Abel, Matt Charman, Steven Spielberg, Joel Coen, Ethan Coen, Alice Krige, Gottfried John\n- Films: Bridge of Spies, Institute Benjamenta\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor, BAFTA Award for Best Supporting Actor, Academy Award for Best Original Screenplay\n- Roles: Soviet intelligence officer, actor, screenwriter, director\n\nFacts:\n- Rudolf Ivanovich Abel, whose real name was Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher, was a Soviet intelligence officer who lived from July 11, 1903 to November 15, 1971.\n- Institute Benjamenta stars Mark Rylance, Alice Krige, and Gottfried John.\n- In 2015, Mark Rylance portrayed Rudolf Abel in the film Bridge of Spies.\n- Mark Rylance won the Academy Award and the BAFTA Award for Best Supporting Actor for his performance as Rudolf Abel in Bridge of Spies.\n- Matt Charman was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Original Screenplay for the 2015 film Bridge of Spies.\n- Bridge of Spies was directed by Steven Spielberg and co-written by Matt Charman, Joel Coen, and Ethan Coen.",
